# Summary

- `Repository` reads, writes, lists, and reconciles project memory documents and their explicitly declared gaps from one validated root directory.
- It extracts declared `.memory` references, allows hierarchical reads only when a parent document explicitly declares the child, and registers generated documents in package and project indexes.

# Dependencies

- Standard library: context, errors, fmt, os, path/filepath, regexp, sort, strings, sync.

# Rules

- Paths must be relative `.memory` files and may not escape the configured root.
- Symlink targets must remain under the resolved memory root.
- The LLM never receives unrestricted file-system access; the repository enforces index declarations.
- Missing `gaps` and `gaps: []` both mean no explicitly declared gaps.
- Writes reject pre-existing symlink ancestors outside the root before creating directories, then use a temporary file and rename under the memory root.
- Per-document and per-index locks serialize read-modify-write updates so concurrent synchronizers retain all references.
- Index reconciliation rewrites generated index references atomically from a supplied document set.
- Generated documents must have closed YAML frontmatter, a matching `type`, valid `gaps`, and a non-empty body before persistence.
